<title>FINLAND: ALCOM PROPOSES CUTTING NOMINAL SHR PRICE.</title>
<headline>ALCOM PROPOSES CUTTING NOMINAL SHR PRICE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish data systems company Alcom Oy said on Monday it was proposing to cut its share capital by lowering its nominal share price to 0.15 markka each from 1.50 markka.</p>
<p>&quot;The lowered amount will be used in full to cover the company's losses,&quot; Alcom said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Debt burdened Alcom has said already earlier its share would not, even in the longer term,  have value as an investment nor would the company be able to pay dividend.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0248, news@Reuters.fi</p>
</text>
